    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="1214" n="1204" xml:id="pg1204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/1–246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-01-02T08:00:00+07:00">January 2, 1946—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. To Acheson for Davis from Marshall. Have approved re Para 3 <hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi> of your 2079, 31 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >29</hi>] December, the Exlm loan of 30 millions for cotton purchase and have
                    approved extension of the unused credit of 12 millions recommended in your 3 <hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi> (see my State 2241, 29 December). Re sale by
                    Maritime Commission of 10 ships (your 3 <hi rendition="#italic">d</hi> (2))
                    approve sale and re your 3 <hi rendition="#italic">e</hi> approve Lend-Lease
                    transfer of 5 ships owned by U. S. Govt against cash reimbursement.
                    [Marshall.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
